    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the full test suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`, the sole runnable test being `AcceptanceTest`).\n\n## Summary\n\nI consolidated all duplicate detection into a single derived `identityKey` and made it a returned field.\n\n**`identityKey` definition** \u2014 `normalizedTelephone + '|' + (email or empty) + '|' + (householdId or empty)`.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a derived `getIdentityKey()` getter that joins the (already-E.164-normalized, stored) telephone, the (already-lower-cased) email or empty string, and the householdId or empty string with `|`. As a derived getter with no persisted column, it needs no DB migration and follows the existing pattern of `displayName`/`initials`/`membershipNumber`.\n\n2. **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `readOnly` `identityKey` string property to the Owner schema. The build regenerates `OwnerDto` from this spec, and MapStruct maps `Owner.getIdentityKey()` into it, so the endpoint now **returns** `identityKey`.\n\n3. **`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014\n   - Moved the `householdId` assignment (for `sharesHousehold=true`) to **before** the duplicate check, so it participates in the key.\n   - Replaced the three separate checks (`isTelephoneInUse` / `isEmailInUse` / `isHouseholdInUse` inside `isDuplicate(owner, sharesHousehold)`) with a single `isDuplicate(owner)` that rejects with 409 only when the new owner's **whole** `identityKey` equals an existing owner's.\n   - Removed the now-unused helper methods and the `java.util.Objects` import.\n\n**Behavior change (as the spec requires):** because the telephone is part of the key, two members of the same household (same `householdId`) with different telephones now have different identity keys and are both allowed; only an exact full-key match is a duplicate. The old standalone telephone/email/household rejections no longer fire independently.\n\nThe `coreRejectsIdentityCollision` acceptance test \u2014 two owners with the same telephone (and both with empty email and no household) producing the same identity key \u2192 409 \u2014 passes.",
